\question{If we hard-code in the manipulation environment the mapping from drawer open / window open to a fixed state and do GCRL will it learn to press the respective buttons?
\question{If so, then how could we plan over the skill to learn the termination condition?}
\question{Then how could we actually learn the mapping from raw state to meaningful things like drawer / window are open / closed?}
\remark{
  This is likely related to [TAMP](garrettIntegratedTaskMotion2021), where maybe we do GCRL on the discrete portion of the state space to learn skills. Although in \em{task and motion planning}, I think the split is actually in the action space?
}
